        "name": "Ilha de Mocambique",
        "description": "A UNESCO island town of Portuguese forts, Swahili stone houses and mosques.",
        "details": "Ilha de Mocambique was the capital of Portuguese East Africa. The Sao Sebastiao fortress sits at the northern tip, and the stone town has mosques, churches and a quiet atmosphere. It is reached by a long causeway. A guide helps with the history.",
