        "name": "Quirimbas Archipelago and Ibo Island",
        "description": "Remote islands with crumbling colonial forts, silver workshops and dhow trips.",
        "details": "The Quirimbas are reached from Pemba by boat or small plane. Ibo Island has a fort, silversmiths and a ghost-town feel, and nearby islands offer white sand and snorkelling. Lodging is simple or luxurious. Check the security situation before travelling.",
